   "note": "Guide Table 7: 24.25 in (61.6 cm) high, 17.25 in (43.82 cm) wide - \"the outer edges of the front-mounting brackets extend the width to 19 in. (48.3 cm)\" - and 20 in (50.8 cm) deep, 20.69 in (52.6 cm) from the front-mounting bracket to the rear. The datasheet gives 17.25 x 24.25 x 21 in (43.82 x 61.6 x 53 cm); the 21 in is the guide's 20.69 in with the handles, and the guide's chassis depth is carried (gap chassis-size). 14 U (guide, \"14 rack units (1/3 rack)\"); 14 U is 622.3 mm, so the 24.25 in body sits inside it. Ears are NOT MODELLED by project convention."
  },
  "color": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "The guide's figures are black and white line drawings and no photograph was found, so the chassis is drawn in a neutral light grey; no colour is stated by a source."
  },
  "gate-1": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "THE FRONT FIGURE PASSES. Figure 3 (g020565, flat) rendered at 450 dpi: the frame with its brackets is 1675 px wide and the body between the fold lines 1524 px, which is 17.25 in at 3.479 px/mm (0.4 percent from the aspect of the 24.25 in height, 3.466 px/mm down: the outline is 617 px at 130 dpi for 616 mm). Positions are good to about a millimetre. Figure 4 draws the same supply row (g020641)."
  },
  "header": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "Figure 3 at 3.479 px/mm: the header plate runs 42.8 to 438.1 mm across and 0 to 36.2 down. LCD window 273.6 to 312.5 mm across and 11.4 to 23.8 down; Menu and Enter buttons centred at 321.2 mm across and 14.9 and 22.1 down; ALM, SYS and MST lamps at 340.5 mm across and 10.3, 18.1 and 25.6 down with their legends to the right; the ESD caution label 356.4 to 375.6 mm across and 12.4 to 25.6 down; the ESD point centred at 380.0 and 19.0; the model name \"EX8208\" centred at 405.9. Where the figure draws the lamps and buttons larger than the registry's parts, the registry's size is used on the same centre."
  },
  "lifecycle": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "Juniper's end-of-life notice (PSN TSB17106, https://www.juniper.net/support/pdf/eol/lod-q22017.pdf, 2017-11-09) lists the EX8200-family XRE200 with a last order date of 2017-06-15 and names the EX9200 as the replacement for the EX8200 line. The EX8208 chassis's own dates were not readable (Juniper's end-of-life table is script-rendered); none is stated."
  },
